    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0111" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–549: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-05T17:00:00+01:00">October 5, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 5—1:43 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3988. In off-record press interview with American correspondents today,
                        Attlee<anchor n="80" xml:id="d109-f1"/> is reported to have said in response
                    to question regarding recognition Chinese Communist Government that (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) British Government would proceed slowly, (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) there were many facets of the problem which
                    needed mature deliberation, including the attitude of <pb facs="0112" n="102"
                        xml:id="pg102"/> Communists toward China’s international obligations, and
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) so far as Nationalist Government is
                    concerned all is not yet lost.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d109-f1" n="80" xml:id="d109-f1-content">
                <p>Clement R. Atlee, British Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
